      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "NULL",
        "right": "auth"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "required.auth_cleared_before_next_send",
      "fine_trace_step": 7,
      "description": "At the start of each `for (net = start_at; ...)` iteration, the vulnerable code reinitializes only the new packet chain. It does not reset the loop-local `auth` and `auth_offset`, so after an earlier send error frees the old AUTH chunk and `continue`s, the next destination iteration inherits a dangling pointer. The fix adds `auth = NULL; auth_offset = 0;` exactly here."
    },
